dialect grammar
grammar stdio.semio.model.diff
extension diff
start line

; The real hand-rolled `SemioModelDiff::print_diff`/`parse_diff` grammar (🔺️diff/🦀️component.rs
; §HandcraftedDiffCodec) -- a single line of space-separated `field=value` tokens, one token per
; present (non-`None`) top-level diff field; an empty diff prints as the empty line. NOT
; envelope-wrapped (unlike the snapshot facet): `encode_diff`/`decode_diff` are the
; print_diff/parse_diff text bytes verbatim. Quoted strings below are literal wire characters;
; unquoted `[...]`/`*(...)` are this grammar dialect's own optional/repetition meta-syntax.
line = token *(SP token)
token = ("spatial=" / "elements=" / "relations=") named-triple

; Shared `🧰️triples::enc_named_triple`/`dec_named_triple` wire shape -- bracket-depth-aware so a
; nested "[...]" payload inside one entry never confuses the outer split (see
; `⚙️engine/🧰️triples/🦀️component.rs`).
named-triple = "[" removed-csv "]" ";" "[" modified-csv "]" ";" "[" added-csv "]"
removed-csv = hex *("," hex)
modified-csv = modified-entry *("," modified-entry)
modified-entry = hex ":" diff-body
added-csv = item *("," item)
diff-body = "[" 1*OCTET "]"   ; per-collection diff-value codec, see 🔺️diff/🦀️component.rs §DiffValueCodecs
item = "[" 1*OCTET "]"           ; full item payload, see 🔺️diff/🦀️component.rs §ValueCodecs
hex = 1*(%x30-39 / %x61-66)      ; hex-encoded string field (id/key), see §Primitives hex_encode
SP = %x20
